# v0.9.1 Phase 8 Task 32 — Lobby.lobbies as the wall target list.
#
# This fixture verifies the SUBSTRATE: Lobby.lobbies holds exactly one
# entry per live realm (the realm's globals object), and indexing it
# returns a real lobby reference.  Every realm registers itself in
# urealm_new, so a single-session run finds exactly one.
#
# The broadcast itself — A's wall reaching B but not A — needs two
# sessions and lives in wall_reaches_other_sessions.chk.

## mode: repl

> {"id":17,"op":"eval","code":"Lobby.lobbies.length()"}
< "id":17 | "kind":"result" | "value":"1"
< "id":17 | "kind":"done"

# Lobby.lobbies.get(0) returns a non-nil Object (the session lobby).
# Use `!=` against nil to coerce to a Bool result without depending
# on closure-name-resolution.
> {"id":18,"op":"eval","code":"Lobby.lobbies.get(0) != nil"}
< "id":18 | "kind":"result" | "value":"true"
